	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Darkshore is a long, grey coast in the north-west of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, across a narrow strait from the great tree {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link}. Its forests are dim even at noon, its beaches are cold, and its hills are full of ruins older than any kingdom of men. The {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} hold it from the small harbor town of {link:auberdine}Auberdine{/link}. They have made it a gate between their new home and the wider world. Yet the land they guard is sick. Its rivers run foul, its beasts have gone mad, and old enemies have come back to the ruins of the elves' own past.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Long before the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, these hills looked down upon the shores of the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link}. Here {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link} raised the twin towns of {link:ameth-aran}Ameth'Aran{/link} and {link:bashal-aran}Bashal'Aran{/link} for her favored Highborne, and set the lord {link:athrikus-narassin}Athrikus Narassin{/link} to govern them from his {link:tower-of-althalaxx}Tower of Althalaxx{/link}. When the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link} ended and the Well was destroyed, the towns fell and the land was torn. What remained became a coast of the new sea. The ruins of {link:ruins-of-mathystra}Mathystra{/link}, once a great bastion of the elves, crumbled in the north. After the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, the night elves raised {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link} off this coast. No chronicle records the year when {link:auberdine}Auberdine{/link} was built.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:auberdine}Auberdine{/link} is a humble town, but it is busy. Ships carry travellers to {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link} and across the sea to the human lands. A new vessel now links it to {link:stormwind-harbor}Stormwind Harbor{/link}, and another sails by way of {link:southshore}Southshore{/link} to {link:menethil-harbor}Menethil Harbor{/link}. The town needs every friend those ships can bring. The {link:blackwood-furbolgs}Blackwood{/link} {link:furbolgs}furbolgs{/link} have turned against the elves. A sickness spreads through the thistle bears and the deer, and it seems to flow from {link:felwood}Felwood{/link} to the east. {link:naga}Naga{/link} hold the ruins of {link:ruins-of-mathystra}Mathystra{/link}. The {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link} digs at the {link:the-master-s-glaive}Master's Glaive{/link}, and a cult of warlocks gathers at the {link:tower-of-althalaxx}Tower of Althalaxx{/link}. When the elder of Auberdine asked {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} for aid, Stormwind had none to give. {link:darnassus}Darnassus{/link} has sent little more.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The night elves of {link:auberdine}Auberdine{/link}.{/b} {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link}, druids and scholars who keep the town, and study the corruption that surrounds it.
• {b}The dwarves.{/b} Miners, smiths and traders from {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}, and the scholars of the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link}, who dig in the south.
• {b}The {link:blackwood-furbolgs}Blackwood{/link} furbolgs.{/b} Once friends of the elves, now maddened and hostile in their camps.
• {b}The {link:naga}naga{/link}.{/b} The Stormscale naga haunt {link:ruins-of-mathystra}Mathystra{/link} and the cave behind {link:cliffspring-falls}Cliffspring Falls{/link}.
• {b}The Greymist murlocs.{/b} They crowd the coast and prey on ships and fishermen.
• {b}The restless dead.{/b} The spirits of the Highborne still wander the ruins of {link:ameth-aran}Ameth'Aran{/link}.
• {b}The moonkin.{/b} They roam the eastern hills, and grow more hostile each season.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Twin Towns.{/b} In the age of {link:azshara}Azshara{/link}, {link:ameth-aran}Ameth'Aran{/link} and {link:bashal-aran}Bashal'Aran{/link} prospered beside the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link}, while the world beneath them slid toward madness.
• {b}The {link:great-sundering}Sundering{/link}.{/b} In the chaos of the war, {link:athrikus-narassin}Athrikus Narassin{/link} promised the people of Ameth'Aran life eternal through his magic. Their spirits have never found rest.
• {b}The Long Sleep.{/b} Many druids followed {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link} into the sleep of the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}. Some who slept have lately awakened, and they find their old homes in ruins.
• {b}The New Home.{/b} After the war against the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}, the night elves made {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link} their home, and {link:auberdine}Auberdine{/link} became its door to the world.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Shore",
			text = [=[• Great sea creatures have been casting themselves upon the beaches of Darkshore in growing numbers. The priestesses of the {link:temple-of-the-moon}Temple of the Moon{/link} have learned that the {link:naga}naga{/link} drive them out.
• A red crystal stands in the eastern hills. Inside it lie fragments of bone and half of a jawbone. The moonkin gather around it, and no one knows why.
• The fishermen of {link:auberdine}Auberdine{/link} no longer take their boats out. They say the murlocs have eaten all the grouper.]=],
		},
	},
})

